From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: flat CPU OPP voltages

Diagnostic only, not for merging. Run every CPU OPP at the 1.8 GHz voltage
so that a frequency change no longer moves vdd_cpu at all. If the resets
under software-ISP load stop, they are caused by the voltage transitions;
if they continue, by the clock switch itself.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [diagnostic experiment]

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN op_a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi op_b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-19 06:23:36.494639300 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-19 06:23:36.516164368 +0200
@@ -281,6 +281,28 @@
 	cpu-supply = <&vdd_cpu>;
 };
 
+/* EXPERIMENT: no voltage transitions at all - see the patch description. */
+&cpu0_opp_table {
+	opp-408000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-600000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-816000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1104000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1416000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1608000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+};
+
 &cru {
 	assigned-clocks = <&pmucru CLK_RTC_32K>, <&cru PLL_GPLL>,
 			  <&pmucru PLL_PPLL>, <&cru PLL_VPLL>;
